2026-09-27T07:42:44.9035558Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9035964Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9036358Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9036488Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9036808Z ================
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9036975Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9037457Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9038022Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9038344Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9038536Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9038938Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9039193Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9039393Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9040006Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9040519Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9041513Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9042307Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9042455Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9043068Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9044014Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9044497Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9044938Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9045580Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9045710Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9045998Z ========
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9136240Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9138571Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9140659Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9141010Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9141723Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9142865Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9143739Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9144574Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9145227Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9145805Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9145957Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9146304Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9146513Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9164553Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9166406Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9167640Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9168958Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:42:44.9169278Z 
